# audit-isa.allow -- reviewed exceptions for scripts/lfs-blfs/cpu-baseline/audit-isa.sh.
# Used only for cases the tool's rules cannot express (variant names, vector-ABI
# names and call-graph-reached helpers are recognised by the tool itself).
# Format: one entry per line, four TAB-separated fields:
#   file <TAB> symbol-glob <TAB> reason <TAB> reviewer and date
#   file        path suffix of the scanned ELF file, e.g. usr/lib/libitm.so.1.0.0
#   symbol-glob shell glob matched against the enclosing function name
#   reason      why baseline (non-AVX) code cannot reach the function
#   reviewer    who reviewed it, and when
# Stale entries (file scanned, no hit) are reported as WARN.
usr/lib/libitm.so.1.0.0	_ITM_*M256	exported transactional-memory entry points compiled for AVX; only AVX-compiled TM code calls them, no caller inside libitm on the baseline path	claude, 2026-11-06 (hand review, docs/verification/rebuild-r2-ch6-2026-11-06.md section 3)
usr/lib32/libitm.so.1.0.0	_ITM_*M256	same as usr/lib/libitm.so.1.0.0 (32-bit build of the same library)	claude, 2026-11-06 (hand review, docs/verification/rebuild-r2-ch6-2026-11-06.md section 3)
usr/lib/python3.14/lib-dynload/_blake2.cpython-314-x86_64-linux-gnu.so	_Py_LibHacl_Hacl_Hash_Blake2b_Simd256_*	CPython HACL* Blake2b AVX2 path, selected at run time: blake2module.c uses Blake2b_256 only when detect_cpu_features reports AVX and AVX2 (has_simd256); no CPUID-free path reaches it	claude, 2026-11-06 (ch7 audit; caveat: CPUID bits only, no XGETBV check, as in CPython)
usr/lib/python3.14/lib-dynload/_blake2.cpython-314-x86_64-linux-gnu.so	update_block	static copy of the Simd256 update helper; the VEX copy is called only from Simd256 functions (checked: 8 callers, all VEX or Simd256)	claude, 2026-11-06 (ch7 audit)
usr/lib/python3.14/lib-dynload/_blake2.cpython-314-x86_64-linux-gnu.so	malloc_raw	static copy of the Simd256 allocation helper; the VEX copy is called only from Simd256 functions (checked: 3 callers, all VEX or Simd256)	claude, 2026-11-06 (ch7 audit)
usr/lib/python3.14/lib-dynload/_hmac.cpython-314-x86_64-linux-gnu.so	_Py_LibHacl_Hacl_Hash_Blake2b_Simd256_*	CPython HACL* Blake2b AVX2 path, selected at run time: hmacmodule.c sets can_run_simd256 only when cpuid reports AVX and AVX2	claude, 2026-11-06 (ch7 audit; caveat: CPUID bits only, no XGETBV check, as in CPython)
usr/lib/python3.14/lib-dynload/_hmac.cpython-314-x86_64-linux-gnu.so	update_block	static copy of the Simd256 update helper; the VEX copy is called only from Simd256 functions (same layout as _blake2)	claude, 2026-11-06 (ch7 audit)
usr/lib/python3.14/lib-dynload/_hmac.cpython-314-x86_64-linux-gnu.so	malloc_raw	static copy of the Simd256 allocation helper; the VEX copy is called only from Simd256 functions (same layout as _blake2)	claude, 2026-11-06 (ch7 audit)
